It has been a while since I have compiled anything on the Alpha and I
have never used gcc on it.  However, the thing that jumps up for me
(that caught me when we ported tons of code from the DEC VAX to the
  Alpha) is that pointers are now 64-bit.  A lot of code sometimes
assumes that point size == 4 bytes (32 bits).  If you are casting
a pointer to an int, it might just be incorrect.  Is there a gcc
switch to force pointer types to 32 bit?

Patrick

